<title>CANADA: Canada body details hard red spring wheat protein.</title>
<headline>Canada body details hard red spring wheat protein.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Thursday detailed the protein content of Prairie hard red spring wheat.</p>
<p>	     No1 Canada Western Red Spring</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba   1,192    14.2 pct  9.4   17.1</p>
<p>Sask.	4,798    12.9 pct  9.1   17.7</p>
<p>Alberta    1,518    12.8 pct  9.1   17.8</p>
<p>W. Cnd.    7,508    13.1 pct  9.1   17.8</p>
<p>	     No2 Canada Western Red Spring</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba   1,498    14.3 pct 10.3   17.9</p>
<p>Sask.	2,209    12.9 pct  8.6   17.1</p>
<p>Alberta	549    12.1 pct  8.6   17.2</p>
<p>W. Cnd.    4,256    13.3 pct  8.6   17.9</p>
<p>	     No3 Canada Western Red Spring</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba     221    13.7 pct 10.6   16.7</p>
<p>Sask.	1,625    12.0 pct  8.5   17.2</p>
<p>Alberta    1,312    11.9 pct  8.0   16.2</p>
<p>W. Cnd.    3,158    12.1 pct  8.0   17.2</p>
<p>	     Canada Western Feed Wheat</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba	67    14.4 pct 11.0   16.3</p>
<p>Sask.	  104    12.5 pct 10.1   14.9</p>
<p>Alberta	246    12.2 pct  9.2   15.6</p>
<p>W. Cnd.	417    12.6 pct  9.2   16.3</p>
<p>	     All Grades</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba   2,978    14.2 pct  9.4   17.9</p>
<p>Sask.	8,736    12.7 pct  8.5   17.7</p>
<p>Alberta    3,625    12.3 pct  8.0   17.8</p>
<p>W. Cnd.   15,339    12.9 pct  8.0   17.9</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
